  "definition": "Standard Error measures the sampling variability of an estimator; smaller standard error means the estimator varies less across repeated samples. It is used in Uncertainty Quantification. It is commonly considered alongside Confidence Interval, Margin of Error, Sampling Distribution.",
  "intuition": "Think of Standard Error as a summary number: it compresses many outcomes into one interpretable value so you can compare models or decisions.",
